sequenceDiagram
  %% Source: crates/shipyard-app/src/device_login.rs (OAuth device flow, RFC 8628).
  actor Person
  participant UI as React UI
  participant Shell as Tauri shell
  participant Host as GitHub or GitLab host
  participant Browser as Web browser
  participant Keychain as OS keychain

  Person->>UI: Click Sign in with the browser
  UI->>Shell: device_login_start(id, click)
  Note over Shell: Read the client id (not a secret) from oauth.env
  Shell->>Host: POST device code request (client id, scope)
  Note over Shell,Host: GitHub: /login/device/code, scope repo.<br/>GitLab: /oauth/authorize_device, scope api mcp,<br/>again with api alone on invalid_scope
  Host-->>Shell: user_code, verification_uri, device_code, interval
  Shell-->>UI: user_code, verification_uri, interval
  UI->>Person: Show the code, with a Copy action
  Person->>Browser: Open verification_uri, type the code, agree
  loop every interval seconds
    UI->>Shell: device_login_poll(id, device_code)
    Shell->>Host: POST token request (device_code grant)
    alt authorization_pending
      Host-->>Shell: error authorization_pending
      Shell-->>UI: Pending
    else slow_down
      Host-->>Shell: error slow_down
      Shell-->>UI: SlowDown, add 5 s
    else access_denied or expired_token
      Host-->>Shell: error
      Shell-->>UI: Denied or Expired
    else token
      Host-->>Shell: access_token (GitLab also refresh_token, expires_in)
      Shell->>Keychain: store the access token for the connection
      Shell->>Keychain: GitLab only: store the refresh state conn:id:oauth
      Shell-->>UI: Authorized
    end
  end
  Note over Shell,Host: GitLab tokens end after 2 hours: Bearer refreshes the token<br/>one request at a time and saves the new refresh token first.
